GPLv2. The additional terms in iSH's LICENSE.IOS also apply; in particular
the iSH copyright holders grant an explicit exception for the conflict
between the GPL and Apple App Store terms of service.

Kelivo itself is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3,
which is compatible with (and a superset of) the GPLv3 terms above.
Corresponding source for iSH-ARM64 is available from the upstream
repository linked above.

The iOS kernel / executor / crash-guard integration in
ios/Runner/Workspace/ is adapted from:

  * Cuplivo (a Kelivo fork) ios/Runner/iSHSandbox/ — AGPL-3.0
  * OpenMinis/MinisApp src/ios/iSH/ — GPL-3.0 (App Store exception via iSH)

2. Alpine Linux rootfs (resources/alpine-rootfs.zip)
----------------------------------------------------
Generated by ios/sandbox/prepare_alpine_rootfs.sh from the official
Alpine Linux aarch64 minirootfs (https://alpinelinux.org), with bash and
coreutils pre-installed from official Alpine APK packages, then converted
to iSH fakefs format (data/ + meta.db). Alpine Linux consists of BusyBox
(GPLv2), musl libc (MIT) and Alpine tooling (MIT) among other packages;
see Alpine's package pages for per-package licenses and source locations.
The rootfs is used solely as the guest userland for the optional Linux
sandbox feature. Nothing is downloaded at runtime — the zip is bundled
in the app and extracted on first launch.
